# GeT-RM reference material, Coriell ID GM17203. GeT-RM consensus diplotype:
# reported as "*1/*2 (*2/*17)" in CDC's table -- the fuller consensus,
# including the 2 methods that test the *17 promoter variant, is *2/*17: a
# real-world compound heterozygote carrying both the *2 no-function variant
# and the *17 increased-function variant simultaneously. THE key real-world
# validation case for this module: genes/cyp2c19.py's module docstring
# argues (from population-genetics and nomenclature evidence) that this
# exact combination should be resolved directly as a compound diplotype
# rather than declined the way DPYD declines its equivalent situation --
# this real GeT-RM lab consensus reporting it as a direct, unflagged
# *2/*17 diplotype (not a phasing caveat) is independent, real-world
# confirmation of that reasoning. Source: Pratt VM et al. 2010, J Mol
# Diagn 12:835-846 (PMID 20889555), as reproduced in CDC's public-domain
# data table
# (https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2024/08/CYP2C19_GeneConsensus.pdf,
# retrieved 2026-08-18). Genotype below constructed from this project's own
# dbSNP-confirmed defining-variant coordinates (genes/cyp2c19.py), not
# redistributed from GeT-RM/Coriell/CDC directly.
#CHROM	POS	ID	REF	ALT	QUAL	FILTER	INFO	FORMAT	SAMPLE1
